WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.970
Carol Peletier's journey is one of the most
wide-ranging in The Walking Dead: She begins

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:11.410
as a battered wife but ends up a queen, a
warrior, and above all, a survivor.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.760
With a spinoff focused on her and Daryl Dixon
on the horizon, there's never been a better

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.220
time to explore her entire story.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.010
Carol has been a survivor for many years.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:28.140
Prior to the story's start, she meets and
marries Ed Peletier, who quickly becomes abusive

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.000
toward both Carol and their daughter Sophia.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.100
When the apocalypse hits, the family tries
to go to Atlanta, only to realize that the

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.019
government is in more of a Napalming mood
than a helping one.

00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:45.420
While stuck in traffic, the Peletiers befriend
Lori, Shane and Carl, who manage to get them

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.219
and a handful of other survivors to a campsite
just outside the city while they figure out

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:51.429
their next move.

00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:56.690
There, Ed's abusive behavior continues, but
now it's happening under the watchful eye

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:00.319
of a former police officer and a group of
like-minded women.

00:01:00.319 --> 00:01:05.360
Shane eventually beats an appropriate amount
of snot out of Ed for slapping Carol in front

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.360
of everyone.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:11.470
As a result of his injuries, Ed isn't exactly
in fighting shape when walkers descend on

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.470
the camp.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.760
He's killed and eventually put down before
becoming a walker by none other than Carol

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.890
herself, marking her first step towards independence.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.430
"I'll do it.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.960
He's my husband."

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:31.201
After the survivors go to the CDC and discover
how dire their situation truly is, they set

00:01:31.201 --> 00:01:32.990
out on the road once again.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:37.360
Unfortunately, they are waylaid when their
RV gives up the ghost.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.590
When a herd of walkers approaches, Carol is
separated from Sophia.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:46.420
Rick tries his best to save her, but he too
is separated from the child in the thick Georgia

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:47.420
woods.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:53.070
It isn't long before the group discovers Sophia
is a walker, locked up with her undead brethren

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.170
in a barn, and Rick is forced to put her down.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:02.160
When the farm they've taken refuge at is overrun
by walkers, Carol isn't much help in the ensuing

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.160
battle.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.409
With no one to guide her and no real fighting
skills to speak of, she must rely on others

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.020
to stay alive.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:13.920
After a brief, failed attempt to replace her
former husband with Daryl, Carol begins to

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.019
understand that her survival is in her hands
and no one else's.

00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:23.530
Season three begins with a minor time jump
that reveals a very new Carol.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.959
She's gained a lot more confidence in the
intervening months and a whole lot of new

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:30.980
skills, ranging from combat to medicine.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:36.230
The loss of her family has hardened her in
a unique way: She is no longer afraid of Ed's

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.810
wrath, nor of losing Sophia.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:43.680
When the survivors hole up in a prison, she
busies herself with first aid and preparations

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.760
to deliver Lori's baby.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:51.290
Unfortunately, a walker attack sets those
plans aside and Carol is trapped alone in

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.540
an overrun part of the prison for several
days.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.730
Fortunately, Daryl finds her and nurses her
back to health, as she once did for him when

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.019
he was injured looking for Sophia.

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:07.120
Their relationship is stronger than it's ever
been when Daryl's older brother, Merle, returns

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.579
to the picture.

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:13.829
Carol sees a lot of Ed in Merle and tries
to encourage Daryl not to lose the man he's

00:03:13.829 --> 00:03:18.529
become, in favor of reverting back to who
he was around his older brother.

00:03:18.529 --> 00:03:23.569
In their final interaction together before
he dies, Merle comments on how different Carol

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:27.879
has become since the last time he saw her
at the camp outside Georgia.

00:03:27.879 --> 00:03:34.409
"Well you don't seem scared of nothing anymore."

00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:35.409
"I'm not."

00:03:35.409 --> 00:03:39.980
When the war with the Governor and Woodbury
begins, Carol proves just how right he is

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:44.109
by encouraging Andrea to assassinate the Governor.

00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:48.650
After the citizens of Woodbury are welcomed
into the prison, Carol begins teaching the

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.559
children how to kill walkers.

00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:55.819
Soon, a flu starts spreading throughout the
prison, and Carol takes it upon herself to

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:59.379
execute two carriers in an effort to stop
the spread.

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:03.620
When Rick figures out what she's done, he
banishes her from the group.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:08.019
As a result, she's away when the Governor
returns to destroy the prison.

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:13.799
In the aftermath of the attack, Carol finds
Tyreese, who has rescued young sisters Lizzie

00:04:13.799 --> 00:04:17.070
and Mika, as well as Lori's baby, Judith.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:21.520
Together, they find their way to a small cottage
where they decide to figure out their next

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.530
move.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:26.970
While there, Lizzie starts to develop a soft
spot for walkers.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:31.310
Carol and Tyreese try to get her to change
her mind after a few encounters with dangerous

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:37.730
walkers, but it's all for naught: Lizzie eventually
kills Mika, convinced that she'll be back

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.350
as a walker and that everything will be fine.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:45.720
What's more, Lizzie confesses that she's planning
to do the same to the baby.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:51.030
Realizing how far gone she is and how much
of a threat she poses to the rest of them,

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:56.920
Carol and Tyreese silently agree to execute
her, which Carol, now a grizzled survivor,

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.190
is willing to do.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.160
They agree to never speak of it again.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.770
"Just… just look at the flowers."

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:10.150
Eventually, the group arrives at Terminus,
and Carol and Tyreese realize that it's crawling

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:13.620
with cannibals who have taken their friends
hostage.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:19.870
Carol launches a one-woman, full-frontal assault
on the compound, almost single-handedly taking

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:24.080
it down with some clever explosions and a
herd of walkers.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.000
Thanks to her bravery, she's welcomed back
to the group, but it isn't exactly the boon

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.550
to survival it once was.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:37.160
With the prison gone and Terminus a proven
sham, the remaining survivors wander the woods

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:38.660
aimlessly.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:43.470
After Beth is kidnapped by a group of vicious
survivors living at a hospital, Carol ends

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.960
up getting hit by a car and taken into the
belly of the beast, where she spends a good

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.850
deal of time unconscious before Daryl and
company rescue her.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:57.700
Their fates change when Aaron arrives and
invites them to be a part of the Alexandria

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:58.700
safe haven.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:03.550
But Carol is skeptical of this apparently
apocalypse-proof community -- she reverts

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:08.950
back to her cheery old housewife persona,
lying in wait for the moment her true new

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.730
nature will be needed.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:15.290
It doesn't take long before she and Rick discover
a man in the community, Pete, is abusing his

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:16.800
wife and kid.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.380
Carol stops baking cookies for a moment to
threaten Pete's life, ultimately turning that

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.700
particular conflict over to Rick, who executes
him.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:32.070
With Rick pretty much in charge of Alexandria,
Carol is forced to abandon her housewife act

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:36.950
when a group of nomadic survivors known as
the Wolves infiltrate the camp and start killing

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.110
its citizens.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:43.550
She dons a disguise and manages to almost
single-handedly stop the invasion, blowing

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.990
her cover within the community forever.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:51.680
Fortunately, her bloodthirsty nature is curtailed
a bit by the arrival of Morgan, who's on a

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:55.500
warrior monk kick and doesn't want to kill
living people.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.590
That attitude, coupled with a new love interest
by the name of Tobin, helps Carol pull back

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.630
from the abyss of violence.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:07.380
Unfortunately, this comes just as the group
fires their first shots in what becomes an

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.360
all-out-war with their toughest enemy yet,
the Saviors.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:16.550
When Rick agrees to take on an outpost held
by their new enemy, Carol finds herself kidnapped

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:22.290
alongside a pregnant Maggie, and she's forced
to use every bit of her cleverness to escape.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:29.660
However, the experience sours her to warfare,
prompting her to leave Alexandria and Tobin.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:33.901
Unfortunately, she's too late, as the Saviors
are already monitoring who goes in and out

00:07:33.901 --> 00:07:35.160
of the colony.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:38.940
She's gravely wounded in a one-versus-five
skirmish.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:43.220
Just when it looks like she's about to be
executed, Morgan arrives to save her.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:47.389
"Will you please just let me go?"

00:07:47.389 --> 00:07:49.780
"It's not your time."

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:55.310
Carol wakes up in the Kingdom, an enigmatic
colony where everyone defers to the judgement

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.150
of King Ezekiel.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:02.080
After some lighthearted bonding with Ezekiel,
she decides she still wants to be alone, but

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:06.090
settles on an abandoned cottage that's not
too far from the Kingdom.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:10.550
She crosses paths with the Alexandrians again
when Rick and the gang seek the Kingdom's

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.150
help in overthrowing the Saviors.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:17.530
Carol has an emotional reunion with Daryl,
during which he lies and tells her that the

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.370
Saviors haven't hurt any of their people.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:25.620
Morgan reveals this to be a lie, however,
and Carol opts to get back to what she does

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.030
best: protect the people she cares about.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:31.170
"We have to get ready.

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:33.690
We have to fight."

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:38.719
By the time she convinces Ezekiel to bring
the Kingdom's forces to Alexandria's aid,

00:08:38.719 --> 00:08:43.860
Negan has managed to breach the walls of the
safe haven and subdue Rick and his fighters.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:49.529
The brash villain is about to execute Carl
as punishment for what he sees as Rick's rebellion

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:53.440
when he's stopped by the united forces of
the Kingdom and the Hilltop.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:58.650
And just like that, Carol finds herself as
a general in the Kingdom's army against the

00:08:58.650 --> 00:08:59.730
Saviors.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:03.720
It doesn't take long for Carol to become one
of the most important fighters in the rebel

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:04.720
army.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:10.110
She leads right beside King Ezekiel as members
of his faction ambush a Savior outpost in

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.480
the hope of obtaining heavy weapons.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.600
Just when the mission seems to have succeeded,
however, the group is cut down by a hail of

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.600
gunfire.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:22.360
Only Ezekiel, Carol and Jerry are left standing.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:27.350
Heroically, Carol makes one more bid to obtain
the weapons, but ultimately decides to save

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:28.830
her allies instead.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.480
These events leave Ezekiel in a spiral of
self-pity.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:37.610
Carol employs tough love to help him out of
it, and the two eventually become makeshift

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.900
parents to a youngster named Henry.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.620
When Negan launches a counter-attack on the
Kingdom, Carol is able to get everyone out

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.620
in time.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:50.680
They retreat to the Hilltop, where they quickly
learn that Negan has also taken out Alexandria.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:55.680
With just one safe haven left, the entire
army prepares for a last stand.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:59.870
A battle ensues, in which Carol is forced
to put Tobin down.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:04.350
In the fray, Henry runs off, forcing Carol
and Morgan to go looking for him, killing

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:06.570
walkers and Saviors along the way.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:12.430
They rejoin Rick's army just in time to witness
all the Saviors' guns backfire, allowing them

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.560
to finally defeat Negan.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:20.450
A year and a half later, Carol reigns as queen
of the Kingdom, having started a romantic

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:22.080
relationship with Ezekiel.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.990
Meanwhile, their colony, the Hilltop, and
Alexandria are doing their best to rebuild

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:31.040
and assimilate the Saviors and their Sanctuary
into their ranks.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:36.100
Unfortunately, things aren't going well, as
constant in-fighting and small acts of defiance

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:38.780
threaten the very terse alliance.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:43.481
Carol personally takes over control of the
Sanctuary briefly, but it doesn't last, as

00:10:43.481 --> 00:10:48.420
several of the more defiant members leave
just before Rick sacrifices himself to unite

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:49.520
the groups.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:54.290
Six years go by, and she and Ezekiel continue
to keep the Kingdom running while raising

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:55.290
young Henry.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:59.600
In an effort to make him more useful, she
escorts him on a trip to the Hilltop so he

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:04.760
can learn blacksmithing and finishes off a
group of former Saviors along the way.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.710
"I swear you'll never see us again."

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:13.020
"I know."

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:17.890
Back at the Kingdom, Ezekiel is busying himself
with a fair that he hopes will convince the

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:22.740
three allied colonies to sign a charter that
will bind them to each other for life.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:27.580
This finally comes to fruition when the Alexandrians
ask the Kingdom to harbor Lydia, the daughter

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:30.120
of the Whisperers' leader, Alpha.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.830
Furious at the kidnapping, Alpha builds a
border that she makes clear the group is never

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:35.930
to cross.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:40.770
Marking the border is a line of heads on spikes
... including Henry's.

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:43.170
Carol is devastated by Henry's death.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:47.681
She leaves Ezekiel shortly after getting the
remaining survivors to the Hilltop, after

00:11:47.681 --> 00:11:50.190
the Kingdom succumbs to deterioration.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:55.290
She sets off to live life by herself as a
fisherwoman, but eventually returns, still

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:57.370
holding a grudge against Alpha.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:12:01.930
When a satellite crash-lands near the Oceanside
colony, they all have to cross the border

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.380
to put out the fire.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.060
This causes Alpha to unleash a relentless
herd upon them.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.540
When they meet for peace talks, Carol pulls
a gun on Alpha.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.880
Fortunately, Alpha is in a forgiving mood.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:18.540
It is revealed that Carol has been taking
pills to keep awake, both as a survival strategy

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.660
and to avoid dreams of what her life could
have been.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:26.120
After the group discovers this, she's taken
back to Alexandria for treatment.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.480
She promptly leaves to take revenge on Alpha's
herd.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:34.380
However, in a shocking twist, it's revealed
that killing the herd is just one part of

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:39.830
Carol's revenge plan: She also frees Negan
from captivity in Alexandria, with the sole

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.460
purpose of having him assassinate Alpha.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:50.260
"So you bring me Alpha's head, and that's
what the people will remember you for."

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:53.970
He succeeds, but Carol isn't able to finish
off the herd.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:58.390
She returns to the survivors and attempts
to sacrifice herself in order to walk the

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:03.720
zombies off a cliff, but she's saved by Lydia
at the last moment, effectively ending the

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.339
Whisperers' reign of terror.

00:13:06.339 --> 00:13:10.900
Carol returns to the camp where she has an
important conversation to fully reconcile

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:16.120
with Daryl, who she's spent the better part
of a year at odds with despite otherwise being

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.360
each other's greatest ally.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.300
Daryl asks if she got what she wanted during
the battle.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:26.920
She admits, without actually saying it, that
she now realizes she never actually wanted

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:29.899
to die, even in a heroic sacrifice.

00:13:29.899 --> 00:13:35.020
With the Whisperers a thing of the past, Carol
is ready to take on all comers with her best

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.110
friend at her side and a new zest for life.

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:42.170
Daryl then asks if she may want to hit the
road for New Mexico, to which she notes that

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.520
there are still things they need to do at
home first.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:50.100
This is the clearest setup for her spinoff
in The Walking Dead franchise beyond the flagship

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.810
series ending after season 11.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:58.240
Norman Reedus told Entertainment Weekly that
he and Melissa McBride's series will be more

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:03.020
of a road show than anything else, meaning
the duo will fight one more battle before

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.360
going off into the sunset together.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.500
